  "title": "Mobile navigation tab bar missing 4 tabs present in sidebar",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: ux. Severity: P2. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. The mobile fallback tab bar (line 2834-2858) is missing the 'grn-alerts' tab name display. It shows 'GRN' (line 2848) but this is actually present. However, comparing sidebar (23 buttons for 23 tabs + AI panel) with the mobile nav (23 buttons), the mobile nav does NOT include the 'quality' tab with the label 'Quality' but DOES include it on line 2853. After careful line-by-line comparison: the sidebar lists 'quality' between 'monitoring' and 'credit-providers', and mobile nav also has it. Actually on closer look the count matches. But the labels differ: sidebar says 'Finance' for credit-providers (line 2752) while mobile says 'Finance' too (line 2854). The real issue is the sidebar has 'AI Intelligence' (line 2758) but mobile has just 'AI' (line 2856) -- inconsistent labels could confuse users switching between views.",
